    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as the cornerstone of the lineup, boasting an elite score of 81.92. His high rating is heavily bolstered by a favorable 16% park factor adjustment and a prime spot in the three-hole against Baz, providing the optimal environment to capitalize on his power upside. While **Caminero** provides the ceiling, our stolen base strategy remains locked on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Kyle Schwarber**, both of whom are projected as high-floor, high-efficiency starts. **Crow-Armstrong** benefits significantly from a 14% dynamic platoon boost against Miller, helping offset the challenge of facing a sub-4.00 xERA starter, while **Schwarber** retains substantial value due to his leadoff role and park factor advantages in the matchup against Leahy.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved keeping **Chase Meidroth** on the bench. With a score of 38.20, he fell just short of our 40.0 floor, primarily due to the poor efficiency profile against McLean\u2019s skill set and a bottom-tier batting order assignment. Conversely, we are banking on **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** to outperform his base projection; his 65.61 score is driven by a massive 17% SP skill advantage against Martinez, though he must overcome the volatility of a seventh-spot order placement. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a start despite a lukewarm 53.21 score; while the platoon disadvantage against Basso suppresses his projection, his elite 0.459 xwOBA is too high to bench in a standard Roto format.\n\nRisks for the day are concentrated in the pending status of **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**; should they shift lower in the order or be rested, their respective scores\u2014currently 48.51 and 64.82\u2014will face downward pressure. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Carson Benge**, whose score of 44.55 makes him the most vulnerable starter in the outfield due to the double-whammy of a tough matchup against Newcomb and a platoon disadvantage. We will keep **Colt Keith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Casey Schmitt** firmly benched, noting that **Schmitt** remains unavailable due to his IL designation, ensuring we focus our daily game-cap allocation on the healthiest, high-leverage assets in the active pool.",
